      <div class="policy__main">
        <header class="policy__head">
          <h1 class="page-head__title">Terms of Use</h1>
          <p class="page-head__lede">These Terms of Use set the queue rules for every ticket taken through Qampus. They keep one student from holding up a line for everyone else, and they tell you what to expect at the window.</p>
          <p class="page-head__updated">Last updated: 27 October 2026.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="policy__body">
          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="who-can-take-a-ticket">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="who-can-take-a-ticket">Who can take a ticket</h2>
            <p>Students signed in with an account. Staff and office heads sign in to run a window, not to take a ticket.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="when-a-window-accepts-tickets">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="when-a-window-accepts-tickets">When a window accepts tickets</h2>
            <p>Only on its open days, from its opening time until 30 minutes before closing. The office head can close a window earlier. The display and each service page show the current state.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="how-many-tickets-you-can-hold">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="how-many-tickets-you-can-hold">How many tickets you can hold</h2>
            <p>One active ticket per service per day, and no more than two active tickets in total. Finish or leave one before taking another.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="the-60-second-wait">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="the-60-second-wait">The 60-second wait</h2>
            <p>After you take a ticket, wait 60 seconds before taking another. Leaving a ticket does not reset that wait.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="your-turn">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="your-turn">Your turn</h2>
            <p>Staff call the next waiting ticket. If your code is called and you do not appear, staff mark a no-show. Two no-shows in one day block new tickets until the next day.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="leaving-a-ticket">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="leaving-a-ticket">Leaving a ticket</h2>
            <p>You can leave a waiting ticket from its page. Once staff call your ticket, you cannot leave it. Talk to the staff at the window.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="location">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="location">Location</h2>
            <p>The system does not ask for or store your location. You can take a ticket from anywhere. The limits above and staff judgement handle misuse.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="what-the-system-stores">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="what-the-system-stores">What the system stores and who sees it</h2>
            <p>Your name, student number, email, password hash, the tickets you take, and an audit record of sign-ins and ticket changes. Passwords are stored as bcrypt hashes. Only signed-in staff and office heads can see the name on a ticket. Ask the CCIT office if a record is wrong. <a href="/privacy">Read the Privacy Policy.</a></p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="what-the-public-display-shows">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="what-the-public-display-shows">What the public display shows</h2>
            <p>Ticket code, service, counter, waiting count, and update time. No name, email, or student number. Staff and office heads can open a named ticket on the staff console.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="fair-use">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="fair-use">Fair use</h2>
            <p>Do not make accounts for other people, automate joins, or hold a ticket you do not intend to use. Staff can mark a ticket no-show. The office head can close a window.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="questions">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="questions">Questions</h2>
            <p>Ask at the service window, or contact the CCIT office.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
